# What kind of auth participant this service is.
#
# Read by the pipeline-catalog auth-conformance gate, which CROSS-CHECKS this
# declaration against what the code actually does and fails on a contradiction
# (`authconformance --explain` prints the full standard).
#
# Declared rather than inferred because inference guesses, and cross-checked
# because a declaration drifts the moment someone adds an outbound call.
#
# inbound-resource-server, and this repo already argued the case in code before
# it declared it:
#
#   internal/middleware/auth.go  builds auth.NewVerifier — the inbound-only
#                                constructor — and its comment notes that
#                                NewServiceClient is the dual-role one, whose
#                                validateConfig "also demands ClientID +
#                                ClientSecret, credentials this service does
#                                not need"
#   internal/config/config.go    lists LEARTECH_AUTH_CLIENT_ID, CLIENT_SECRET,
#                                TARGET_AUDIENCE and SERVER_URL as inertAuthEnv:
#                                variables it reads NO meaning from, reported at
#                                boot rather than silently ignored
#
# A service holding CLIENT_ID/CLIENT_SECRET it never spends looks like it
# carries an identity it does not, which is how inert credentials reach charts
# and how an operator comes to believe a variable is load-bearing. This file
# makes the gate check that story rather than trusting it.
type: inbound-resource-server
